    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Each approach has unique benefits, but traditional braces remain the most reliable for full control and proper alignment."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The Role of Regular Adjustments"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Braces treatment isn’t a one-time setup; it’s a slow, steady process guided by precision. Every few weeks, you’ll visit your orthodontist for regular adjustments, where small wire tweaks help your teeth continue to move in the right direction. These sessions are the heartbeat of your orthodontic treatment, ensuring progress stays on track and your dental alignment remains balanced."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "During these visits, your orthodontist checks wire tension, rebonds any loose metal brackets, and ensures that braces work as expected. Sometimes new rubber bands are added or adjusted to improve bite alignment. Even a millimeter’s change in pressure can influence how crooked teeth begin to settle into proper alignment."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Skipping visits might seem harmless, but it slows down the process. Braces fix crooked teeth only through consistent force; each appointment refreshes that force. Think of it like tuning a piano; without tuning, notes drift off. Similarly, without regular tightening, your teeth straightening rhythm breaks."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Some patients experience mild soreness after adjustments, normal signs that the teeth braces are doing their job. That tenderness fades in a day or two. A quick rinse with warm salt water usually helps. Feels like real progress, honestly."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Over time, these minor tweaks shape your teeth toward their desired position. You may not notice the change week by week, but compare photos every few months, and the difference surprises most patients. Consistency matters here more than anything."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The Results: What You Can Expect"
    },
    {
      "type": "img",
      "src": "../assets/blog/how-braces-can-correct-crooked-teeth-a-complete-guide/02.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "title": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Once treatment ends, the transformation speaks for itself. Braces on crooked teeth don’t just line things up; they rebuild your smile and restore balance between your upper and lower teeth."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "After your braces are removed, you’ll notice:"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Evenly spaced teeth with no more overlapping or crowding."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "A balanced bite that makes chewing smoother and speech clearer."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Improved oral hygiene Brushing and flossing become easier, lowering cavities and gum disease risk."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "A more confident, healthier smile that feels natural."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Many patients say they expected just a cosmetic change but noticed more comfort while eating or speaking. The mouth feels lighter, cleaner, and almost unfamiliar at first. That’s when it hits: years of tightness and uneven pressure are gone."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Beyond looks, properly aligned teeth protect long-term dental health. They wear evenly, keep gums cleaner, and prevent future problems like chipping or jaw strain. The payoff of months of orthodontic care is a smile that feels easy not forced. Sometimes it’s those quiet improvements, like biting into an apple without a thought, that make patients realize how far they’ve come."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Final Thoughts"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Braces fix crooked teeth safely and steadily, no matter the age. With consistent care, timely visits, and proper hygiene, braces work to give you the beautiful smile you deserve. At Dr Dante Gonzales Orthodontics, we guide every step from initial consultation to the final retainer ensuring your orthodontic treatment brings both properly aligned teeth and lasting comfort. Schedule a free consultation and start your journey to a healthier, confident smile today."
    },
