    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "1. Can braces fix crooked teeth in adults? Yes, adult braces work effectively. With healthy gums and good bone support, orthodontic treatment can move teeth at any age safely. 2. Which braces are best for crooked teeth? Metal braces suit most cases. For aesthetics, choose ceramic braces, lingual braces, or clear aligners depending on visibility preference and treatment plan. 3. How long does it take to fix crooked teeth? Treatment takes about 12–24 months depending on misalignment severity and how well you follow cleaning and orthodontist visits. 4. Can braces fix crooked bottom teeth only? Yes. Some orthodontic treatments target crooked bottom teeth or specific arches. The orthodontist decides if upper correction is needed for balance. 5. Is jaw pain normal during braces treatment? A little jaw pain or tightness is common when the braces start to move teeth. It eases as the mouth adjusts and alignment stabilizes."
    }
